<title>RUSSIA: Russian Rosneft in deal for 17,000 bpd Iraqi oil.</title>
<headline>Russian Rosneft in deal for 17,000 bpd Iraqi oil.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian oil firm Rosneft has signed a contract with Iraq's State Organisation for Marketing of Oil (SOMO) to buy the equivalent of 17,000 barrels per day of Iraqi oil over six months, a Moscow oil official said on Monday.</p>
<p>Yuri Agababov, deputy director of Zarubezhneft, the Russian company coordinating all Russian oil purchases from Baghdad, said Rosneft would buy its oil in four lots and would most likely lift from Iraq's southern terminal Mina al-Bakr.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
